BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehousto
 n.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Calendar-2-scaled.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehouston.org/wp-content/upload
 s/2026/05/Calendar-2-scaled.jpg
UID:o7KNt6LyNyUpU-LoOkuG9
SUMMARY:Everyday Self-Defense: Building Confidence Through Boundaries & De-
	escalation
DTSTAMP:20260812T042900Z
DTSTART:20260813T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:In this self-defense session\, the instructor\, Sarah Degar\, J
	iu Jitsu black belt\, and architect at GSMA\, will share her unique approa
	ch to personal safety\, focusing on two key objectives: setting boundaries
	 and de-escalating potential uncomfortable situations. After demonstrating
	 key techniques\, attendees will partner up to practice\, with the instruc
	tor offering guidance to each group. \nThe first part of the session will 
	teach participants how to navigate unwanted physical contact in everyday s
	ituations\, particularly with people they know. In professional and social
	 contexts\, it can be challenging to assert boundaries—especially for many
	 women who already worry about being perceived as “unreasonable.” The inst
	ructor will address simple strategies to divert this contact to maintain c
	omfort and autonomy. For example\, a colleague approaches for a hug or put
	s an arm around the waist to pose for a photo. Attendees will be empowered
	 to practice subtle yet effective ways to establish personal space without
	 confrontation. \nThe second part of the session will address more serious
	 scenarios\, where the potential for physical harm exists. Whether the con
	cern comes from someone familiar or not\, de-escalation is crucial. Partic
	ipants will learn techniques to create and maintain a safe distance\, keep
	 a steady stance to avoid being easily pushed or pulled\, and how to break
	 free from various types of holds. The session will wrap up with interacti
	ve games designed to reinforce the skills learned\, making it fun and memo
	rable while encouraging participants to continue practicing on their own. 
	\n\nDoors Open 5p\nClass 5:30p – 6:30p\nSocial to follow\n\nAdvanced Regis
	tration Required. \n \n\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/everyday-se
	lf-defense-building-confidence-through-boundaries-de-escalation/\n\nFrom A
	IA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/everyday-self-defense-building-co
	nfidence-through-boundaries-de-escalation/
LOCATION:Third Ward Jiu-Jitsu\, 2016 Emancipation Ave\, Houston\, TX\, 7700
	3\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT3H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://architecturehousto
 n.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/The-Swap.webp
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://architecturehouston.org/wp-content/upload
 s/2026/08/The-Swap.webp
UID:TKU-FIRRDn9RlGjg49-Ee
SUMMARY:The SWAP: Trade Notes. Make Connections
DTSTAMP:20260812T042900Z
DTSTART:20260813T183000Z
DESCRIPTION:Do you have study materials collecting dust? A study strategy t
	hat’s helped you succeed? Are you looking for an accountability partner or
	 extra motivation on your licensure journey? \n\nJoin HNOMA for The Swap\,
	 an interactive event designed to connect aspiring architects\, exam candi
	dates\, and recently licensed professionals. Exchange study materials\, sh
	are test-taking strategies\, and build a supportive community of peers nav
	igating the A.R.E. process.\n\nThe Houston Chapter of NOMA and LeaderFlow 
	are partnering to host this two-part experience. The evening will begin wi
	th a fireside-style panel discussion moderated by LeaderFlow\, featuring p
	rofessionals who will share insights\, lessons learned\, and practical adv
	ice from their licensure journeys. Attendees will then break into smaller 
	groups for facilitated discussions\, providing an opportunity to ask quest
	ions\, exchange resources\, and connect with others at various stages of t
	he A.R.E. process.\n\nWhether you’re exploring licensure for the first tim
	e\, actively studying for exams\, or recently licensed and looking to give
	 back\, we encourage you to join us.\n\nThere’s something valuable for eve
	ryone at The Swap.\n\nPanelists\nShreya Patel\, Harrison Kornberg\nTim Uzo
	igwe\, Perkins & Will\nJaniece Williams\, Leaderflow\nJavier E. Guerrero\,
	 Martinez Architects\nFallon Barrett\, City of Houston\n\nRegister here \n
	\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/the-swap-trade-notes-make-connecti
	ons/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/the-swap-trade-notes-make-connect
	ions/
LOCATION:Perkins & Will\, 1001 McKinney St.\, Houston\, TX\, 77002\, United
	 States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
